A||||23||'75 383 vette||V-8 conversion for Fiero!!||||14||
Z||000000||'75 383 vette||11-04-2001||12:23 AM||||Howdy fellas...<BR>I just jumped over to yer forum from corvetteforum.com...<BR>I've got a co-worker who has been buggin' me on what to do with his Fiero...<BR>He's got an '86 w/ a four-cylinder.<BR>He is COMPLETELY ignorant when it comes to mechanical devices.<P>Now, two weeks ago, after giving this guy unheeded advice for two months, I went over to a PC at work and tried your web address...<BR>I figured, Corvette owners aren't the only ones who are fanatical about their cars, and there must be some website dedicated to these Fieros...<BR>Well, on the first try, I found you guys.<BR>Your forum is just like my Corvette forum (for the most part), and I'm sure there is a great load of info and knowledge available here that is just waiting to be tapped.<P>I did a search on "crate motor", figuring I could give him advice from you guys on getting a crate instead of having a mechanic rebuild his 4 banger (not to mention that this "mechanic" hasn't rebuilt a motor since who-knows-when, and especially a four-cylinder).<BR>Well I found the MOTHER LOAD!!<BR>Not even twenty minutes away from work... there is this place which makes a V-8 conversion for Fieros!!<BR>I've read about Fieros running Northstar V-8's, but never a Chevy.<P>Now, he's dropped off his car at this shop in Barrington, Il, and they're gonna set him up with a new $1289 crate from GM, and install a new interior.<BR>I'm glad for him... but now I'm also a little jealous...<BR>I'm considering going out and getting my own Fiero to drop a big ol' chevy into.<P>Have any of you fellas with V-8's broken any driveline parts??<BR>I'd like to drop my current 383 into a Fiero.  With about 420-440 hp, I'm sure I'd be able to burn some rubber.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I'll update you folks on his V-8 conversion as I get the info... plus he told me he's got a sign-on here (unless he lied).<P>One more thing... that company, what's their name, and what is yer guy's opinion of them?<P>------------------<BR>1975 'Vette:<BR>1978 4 bolt main block, 3.75" Eagle forged crank, Clevite 77 race bearings, Comp Cams XE268, Rpm Air-Gap, Holley 4777, petronix hi-po module, Accel 47,000 volt coil, Accel 300+ 8.8 plug wires, TH400 w/ shift kit, 3.70 rear w/ posi, fiberglass monoleaf spring, 2.5" true dual exhaust w/ Walker hi-flo cats, Hooker super comp headers...<BR>Plus more...<p>[This message has been edited by '75 383 vette (edited 11-04-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||pHoOl||11-04-2001||12:27 AM||||I"m guessing that you're talking about V8archie.  He is the man!!  Never bought anything from him but when i do a v8 conversion i'm givin him a call.  seems as though he's been in the business the longest, and has a lot of satisfied customers on this board.<P>try..  <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>Kills:<BR>97 Neon R/T<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>         <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||'75 383 vette||11-04-2001||12:31 AM||||Thanx!!!<BR>That's the company all right!<P>BTW, when my co-worker stopped in there and asked for the work to be done, the dude said to him," how about I pay you $3,000.00 for the car and you just walk away??"<BR>My co-worker said NO WAY.<BR>He's dead-set on getting this car fixed to his liking.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever3000||11-04-2001||12:44 AM||||I'm curious to find out what your friend's username is here.<P>V8Archie is like the shark hunter guy on the first Jaws movie... :scratches fingernails on chalkboard: "All know me, know what I do. I'll fix this fish for ya.  Fix him good.  Stick a brand new 350 V8 in 'im and land it on your driveway.  But I don't do it for free... "<P>There are some 383 owners here, like Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"> and I think somebody else has one.  I personally can't talk the talk about engine swaps, but you're gonna get some interesting replies here so keep coming back.  Welcome!<BR>||||reg||1
