Z||000007||FieroKyle||11-04-2001||01:19 AM||||We welcome Corvette owners in open arms until they start calling the Fiero a leser Corvette, lol. J/K, no flames intended on my behalf. We all have the same opinions on stuff and agree usually. Welcome to the forum. Its amazing on what you can do to a Fiero, and many people respect that. Its not just a lifeless hunk of plastic that had a few fires like every outsider claims that don't know the truth. V8Archie is the man and he can turn oridnary Fieros to run with the Vettes on the quarter mile, (well most anyway, we have to exclude the z06 and other high performance models). But anyways off the subject, this is a great place find info yada yada. <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||GTFiero1||11-04-2001||01:23 AM||||im gonna have to refer you to this thread     <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011221.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/011221.html</A>     he had the top chopped 3 inches by <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>  and a LT1 with 350hp was installed by archie too!<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
Z||000009||sloth85GT||11-04-2001||01:28 AM||||Archie is my god........<P>well not yet, but when I order his kit he will be  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">     <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||Oreif||11-04-2001||01:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by '75 383 vette:<BR><B>Hey Oreif...<BR>Ever go to any of the 1/4 mile track around??<BR>I'm thinking my car might finally be ready to take her first run down a strip!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I use to go to Great Lakes when my cousin was racing back in the 80's. For me the track has to be 1/2 mile or longer and lots of tight corners.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Archie built a drag racing Fiero. SB Chevy, Dual Quads, Open headers, etc. He's going to do some 1/4 mile blasts in the spring.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000011||'75 383 vette||11-04-2001||01:52 AM||||Yeah, I think the hot-roddin' bug is alive and well these days...<BR>Its just that people are using differant cars other that the old '60's USA cars.<P>To me... if you did the work yourself, your work made the car go faster/ handle better/ scare little children  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> / you're a hot rodder...<P>BUT if yer just gonna put a big 'ol cessna wing on the back, with a big 'ol fart tube chrome exhaust tip, and all kind of graphics on the car (like you've got corporate sponsership) AND THE THING IS STILL SLOW...<BR>YER JUST A POSUER!!<P>Okay, okay,   I give in...<BR>When the exterior mods are TASTEFUL and not too gaudy, and if those fart tubes make you go faster, that's cool too.<P>I realize not everybody (including myself) has $40 thou lying around that they can invest in a car, but if you can get down and dirty, and work on the car yourself, and make it better, I REALLY respect that, ricer, domestic, custom, antique, etc...<P>I don't have much patience for the 40ish year-old guy in his mid-life crisis with a deep wallet who sends his car out to be hot-rodded by somebody else, then when you ask him what's been done to the car, he tries to act secretive and claim he doesn't want to divulge his combo... ITS BECAUSE HE DON'T HAVE A FRIGGIN CLUE WHAT HE'S GOT!!!  (see 96 and up corvette owners)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Dave Gunsul||11-04-2001||04:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B>the Vettes on the quarter mile, (well most anyway, we have to exclude the z06 and other high performance models). <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Umm, I don't mean to pick on you Kyle but<BR>Archie can easily put a Z06's engine into a <BR>Fiero and with less weight and more traction<BR>the Fiero would easily be faster.<BR>As a matter of fact I can think of two V8 Fieros that Archies done right here in Illinois that would probably make a Z06 owner<BR>throw his keys down and walk away from his car in shame. Both are around the 450 HP range if not more.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
