Z||000018||Formula88||11-04-2001||02:17 PM||||Hey, 383, welcome to our little corner of the universe!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>We've got lots of 12 and 13 second daily driver Fieros around here.  Everything from N20 2.8V6's, 3800SC (Grand Prix GTP engine), to Northstars and loads of V8's.  Check out this thread from V8Archie - he's putting a ZZ4 crate engine with TPI into a re-bodied Fiero.  The job's already done, and the dude got 26mpg on his trip home (after break in) and the power is incredible.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014783.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014783.html</A> <P> ||||reg||10
Z||000019||fix||11-04-2001||02:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B>There are some 383 owners here, like Tina   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif">  and I think somebody else has one. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That would be me!!  Well, I'm still working on installing my 383, but I keep finding more stuff that I want to do to the car that puts me behind schedule. These damn little cars are addictive.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
