Z||000021||Jim_Sprang||11-04-2001||11:43 PM||||Yes, axles are a sore spot with me!  Did three in one summer - seven in total.  Finally had a set built in Windsor, on my third season with them so far so good.  I tore apart two rear ball joints before I switched to the 88 suspension.  But I built the car in 95 have more than 30KM on the conversion and still use it as my daily driver!  <P>------------------<BR>86 SE, 88 suspension<BR>6.6 Liter SBC, Subframe Connectors, Poly Bushings,17X8 MHTs  with 235 45 17 front, 245 45 rears, Lots more!||||reg||1
Z||000022||FieroKyle||11-04-2001||11:49 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dave Gunsul:<BR><B> Umm, I don't mean to pick on you Kyle but<BR>Archie can easily put a Z06's engine into a <BR>Fiero and with less weight and more traction<BR>the Fiero would easily be faster.<BR>As a matter of fact I can think of two V8 Fieros that Archies done right here in Illinois that would probably make a Z06 owner<BR>throw his keys down and walk away from his car in shame. Both are around the 450 HP range if not more.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, I know that, just most people don't have the money for an LS6 engine. Most of them are just a regular 350. Putting a Z06 is not too different than putting in any other 350 or LT1, just cost a lot more. I don't doubt it for one second. Again the potential goes as far as the wallet goes.<P><p>[This message has been edited by FieroKyle (edited 11-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||artherd||11-05-2001||01:33 AM||||Welcome to the Fourm!!<P>Yeah, we're all just a bunch of car nuts who like to scare small children (hehh, love that defenition of 'hot rod'  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Archie has done somewhere over 1500 cars, and I haven't heard of a driveline failure (that wasn't clearly caused by improper clutch instilation/failure-because-it's-not-a-centreforce, etc.)<P>Pretty amazing, actually.  Considering we have at least a dozen fourm members running in excess of *400horsepower* in their cars!!<P>GM made the Fiero about eight times stronger than it ever needed to be, so it holds up pretty well (the 88s being the strongest just due to rear link suspension and solid engine cradles.)<P>Yep, Archie will toss that 383 into a Fiero for ya, and it'll just about be a Corvette Indy (mid-engine corvette prototype  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Most of us really like Corvettes (I myself one day want to put an LT5 into an early 1950s gen1  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">, infact we like them so much, that we usually lift their LT1 motors for our cars!<P>Cheers man, hope you enjoy the fourm!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
